lok: a missing font names the font drawn instead

LOK_CALLBACK_FONTS_MISSING listed the families a document asks for
and the system lacks, but not what was drawn in their place. The
font-mapping data collected at load holds it. The payload now adds
"fontsused", one array per entry of "fontsmissing", with the
families that drew it (style dropped), so a client can say "Nowhere
Sans, shown in Liberation Sans" (Ely C19.1, PRD: the substitution
rule must be visible).
--- a/desktop/inc/lib/init.hxx
+++ b/desktop/inc/lib/init.hxx
@@ -255,7 +255,8 @@
         std::shared_ptr< LibreOfficeKitDocumentClass > m_pDocumentClass;
         std::map<size_t, std::shared_ptr<CallbackFlushHandler>> mpCallbackFlushHandlers;
         const int mnDocumentId;
-        std::set<OUString> maFontsMissing;
+        // Ely: each missing font, and the families drawing it.
+        std::map<OUString, std::set<OUString>> maFontsMissing;
 
         explicit LibLODocument_Impl(css::uno::Reference<css::lang::XComponent> xComponent,
                                     int nDocumentId);
--- a/desktop/source/lib/init.cxx
+++ b/desktop/source/lib/init.cxx
